  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a fix plan, but I haven't changed any code because plan mode is on. The tool for requesting plan approval isn't available in this session, so I'm asking here instead.\n\n**Cause:** `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py:754` returns `bound - dir` when the bound is open (`min_open` or `max_open`). `convert` passes `dir=1` for values below the minimum and `dir=-1` for values above the maximum, so `dir` points into the range. Subtracting it moves the result out of the range instead.\n\nFor example, `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-5` returns `-1`, which is invalid. It should return `1`.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n- Change `bound - dir` to `bound + dir` at `src/click/types.py:754`.\n- Add tests in `tests/test_types.py` for clamped `IntRange` with open bounds. For example, `min=0` open should give `1`, and `max=10` open should give `9`.\n- Run `pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\some-users-report-that-lexical-alpaca.md`. Tell me to proceed and I'll make the change.",
